    "review": "Approved by the owner in the decision pull request for #234, accepting that the upstream target image carries no attestation and that Codex 0.155.0 had not yet run a task through the gateway. Changes from the #226 approval: native is upstream's from-source build of the same 10.10.0 source, the Linux x86-64 executable fd5ffef2d825d9035b3956b0026911a22e2c1b56f7fa205dd00310cfe88aeff5 carried by its published target image (pinned below), replacing the release archive's d0c84ffbafa731ef7fa6b61f87af9c000cc4e5b4d2e0d3b7df461fd239bb923e; restic is unchanged; and the asset now runs on Codex 0.155.0 with Node.js v24.21.0, replacing Codex 0.153.4 with Node.js v22.23.2, as the adopted environment dotnet-r2 (manifest SHA-256 8d1168f339f599d1719dcdc4f4cae8c44966d3f642a3a7e6a3cf81f7e3c66f6e) carries them. Verified: generate.sh, run with that executable copied out of the pinned image, reproduces the unchanged asset bytes twice in clean environments and native admits them with an exact round trip; describe.py reads the unchanged structure below (six executable nodes, builtin.git-delivery.pr@2 with the v2/pr receipt (ready, ci_failed, conflict, repair_required) whose non-ready outcomes route to delivery_repair, the 10-iteration change loop, no node deadlines, gateway connections on every agent node, GH_TOKEN only on delivery, and the default consider pull-request feedback); the asset's graph, runtime, policy and connections are unchanged."
